{"effort": "high", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "recorded_at": "2026-10-29T04:13:20Z", "response": {"container": null, "content": [{"thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"caller": {"type": "direct"}, "id": "toolu_01VzL38E161AF1VrjzXXKK43", "input": {"claims": [{"citations": ["E-004426"], "quotes": [{"event_id": "E-004426", "field": "logon.type", "text": "remote_interactive"}, {"event_id": "E-004426", "field": "source.ip", "text": "192.0.2.21"}], "text": "it-ops2 logged on to WS-07 by remote interactive (RDP-style) logon from 192.0.2.21 at 02:42 UTC, outside normal hours."}, {"citations": ["E-004425"], "quotes": [{"event_id": "E-004425", "field": "process.command_line", "text": "net.exe localgroup Administrators user07 /add"}, {"event_id": "E-004425", "field": "process.parent.name", "text": "mmc.exe"}], "text": "Two minutes later, net.exe launched from mmc.exe added user07, the regular user of WS-07, to the local Administrators group."}, {"citations": ["E-004466", "E-004465"], "quotes": [{"event_id": "E-004465", "field": "process.command_line", "text": "net.exe localgroup Administrators svc-backup /add"}, {"event_id": "E-004466", "field": "source.ip", "text": "192.0.2.21"}], "text": "The same account and source IP did the same thing on SRV-01 about 30 minutes earlier, adding svc-backup to local Administrators. This points to a deliberate multi-host privilege change, which could be admin work or lateral movement."}, {"citations": ["E-001515", "E-001491"], "quotes": [{"event_id": "E-001491", "field": "dns.question.name", "text": "intranet.corp.example"}], "text": "The WS-07 events show no malware, no unusual child processes and no suspicious outbound network activity. The only network events are user07's normal Outlook and intranet traffic, so there is no sign of compromise beyond the privilege changes."}], "confidence": "medium", "injection_reports": [], "recommended_actions": [{"action": "open_ticket", "citations": ["E-004425", "E-004465", "E-004426", "E-004466"], "id": "ACT-001", "reason": "Ask the client to confirm whether it-ops2, from 192.0.2.21, made the 02:13 and 02:44 UTC admin group changes on SRV-01 and WS-07, and whether a change request covers them. If it wasn't them, reset the password and disable the account, and remove user07 and svc-backup from Administrators.", "target": "it-ops2"}], "summary": "At about 02:44 UTC, it-ops2 logged on to WS-07 over RDP from 192.0.2.21. About two minutes later they used mmc.exe and net.exe to add user07 to local Administrators. The same account and source IP did the same thing on SRV-01 at about 02:13, adding svc-backup. The pattern is consistent with either an IT admin doing planned work or a compromised admin account. The logs don't show a change ticket or any malware or C2 activity. Someone needs to ask the client whether it-ops2 made these changes and whether they were authorized.", "verdict": "needs_human"}, "name": "submit_verdict", "type": "tool_use"}], "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011CgVsqZWDi7PdnRXRHe8Vx", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 1046}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1046, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6371, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1231, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 95}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}, "source": "live", "tool_results": [], "turn": 5}
